# Scaladoc for Spark connector types

When writing or completing **class-level** Scaladoc on a class or trait that extends a built-in Spark Data Source V2 SPI type used to build a connector, start the comment with this opening line, then follow `scaladoc-classes` (description remainder, construction guidance, `@param`, `@since`). Methods still follow `scaladoc-methods`.

## Opening line

Use this template, linking the **primary** Spark SPI type:

```
Concrete implementation of Spark's connector [[SparkType]] for ARCGIS datasource
```

Replace `SparkType` with the Spark type that defines the class's connector role, for example `[[Table]]`, `[[ScanBuilder]]`, `[[Scan]]`, `[[Batch]]`, `[[TableProvider]]`, `[[PartitionReader]]`, `[[PartitionReaderFactory]]`, or `[[InputPartition]]`. The same formula applies to any other type under `org.apache.spark.sql.connector` or `org.apache.spark.sql.sources` that is part of the connector SPI.

This opening line is the first line of the class description and counts toward the 10-line description limit in `scaladoc-classes`.

## Which Spark type to link

- Link the primary connector role, not mix-ins. `ArcgisTable extends Table with SupportsRead` → `[[Table]]`, not `[[SupportsRead]]`.
- Ignore non-SPI Spark types such as `Logging`.
- If the type extends several SPI interfaces, pick the one that names its role in the Spark connector lifecycle.

## Do / don't

```scala
// ❌ BAD — generic description; missing the required opening line
/**
 * Spark table for reading ArcGIS feature layers.
 *
 * @param tableSchema Spark schema of the feature layer
 * @since 0.1.0
 */
class ArcgisTable(...) extends Table with SupportsRead

// ❌ BAD — opening line present, but shared class rules not applied
/**
 * Concrete implementation of Spark's connector [[Table]] for ARCGIS datasource
 * @param tableSchema
 * @param tableProperties
 */
class ArcgisTable(...) extends Table with SupportsRead

// ✅ GOOD — opening line, then @param and @since from scaladoc-classes
/**
 * Concrete implementation of Spark's connector [[Table]] for ARCGIS datasource
 *
 * @param tableSchema     Spark schema of the feature layer
 * @param tableProperties table options used to configure reads
 * @since 0.1.0
 */
class ArcgisTable(
  private val tableSchema: StructType,
  private val tableProperties: CaseInsensitiveStringMap
) extends Table with SupportsRead
```

```scala
// ✅ GOOD — ScanBuilder; extra description is allowed after the opening line
/**
 * Concrete implementation of Spark's connector [[ScanBuilder]] for ARCGIS datasource
 *
 * Builds an [[ArcgisScan]] from the table schema and read configuration.
 *
 * @param readConfig   options that control how the feature layer is queried
 * @param tableSchema  Spark schema of the table to scan
 * @since 0.1.0
 */
class ArcgisScanBuilder(...) extends ScanBuilder
```

## Notes

- Do not invent a different first sentence for these types; always use the template above.
- After the opening line, do not skip `@param` / `@since` (or construction guidance) required by `scaladoc-classes`.
- This rule does **not** apply to classes that only use Spark types as fields or method signatures without extending a connector SPI type.
- Method Scaladoc is unchanged; see `scaladoc-methods`.
